# Spicy Meal — environment template for the repository root: the admin console
# (Vite, src/) and the build tooling. This is the only root template.
#
# Copy it to .env.local for local development (`.env*` is gitignored, except this
# file). Vite reads VITE_* from there at build time; deployed builds take the same
# names from the Vercel project. The Expo customer app does NOT read this file —
# see the pointer below, and do not add EXPO_PUBLIC_* values here.
#
# EVERYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` OR `EXPO_PUBLIC_` IS COMPILED INTO THE CLIENT
# BUNDLE AND IS PUBLIC. Only ever put credentials here that are designed to be
# public client credentials (CLAUDE.md §9). The Supabase service-role/secret key,
# provider secrets (Lazywait, WhatsApp/Meta, SMTP, payment), the Meta app secret
# and the SMTP password are NOT client values: they live in Supabase
# (`integration_settings`, Vault, Edge Function secrets) and must never appear in
# a `.env` that a bundler can read.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin console (Vite) — src/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase project. The publishable key (sb_publishable_...) and the legacy anon
# JWT are both public, RLS-scoped credentials by design. The publishable key wins
# when set; the anon key is the fallback until Supabase retires it (end-2026,
# docs/SUPABASE_API_KEYS.md).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR-PROJECT-ref.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="YOUR-anon-public-key"

# Maps. The current provider is Google (docs/MAPS.md). Set it explicitly: when
# VITE_MAP_PROVIDER is unset, src/lib/map.ts falls back to mapbox, which has no
# token configured. The browser key is public by design but must be restricted
# in Google Cloud; the map and the address search need Maps JavaScript API and
# Places API (New). Keep the real key in .env.local and the Vercel environment,
# never in Git.
VITE_MAP_PROVIDER="google"
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY="YOUR-browser-restricted-google-maps-key"

# Mapbox remains supported by the provider abstraction as an alternative. To use
# it, set the provider to mapbox and supply a PUBLIC pk.* token, URL-restricted in
# the Mapbox dashboard; a token that does not start with pk. is treated as
# unconfigured.
# VITE_MAP_PROVIDER="mapbox"
# VITE_MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN="pk.YOUR-mapbox-public-token"
# VITE_MAPBOX_STYLE_URL="mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12"

# Sentry (surface 'admin-web'). A DSN is a public ingestion identifier; an empty
# DSN disables reporting entirely. Set VITE_SENTRY_DEV=1 to actually send from a
# local dev server. SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN is NOT a client value (see the build-time
# section below): never prefix it with VITE_.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=""
VITE_SENTRY_ENV=""
VITE_SENTRY_DEV=""

# Payment/refund code is frozen while the final provider is selected (CLAUDE.md
# §6). Do not create VITE_ payment-secret variables from old documentation.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Customer app (Expo) — NOT HERE. See apps/mobile/.env.example
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Expo app does not read this file, and putting EXPO_PUBLIC_* values here
# fails SILENTLY rather than loudly, which is why this section is a pointer
# rather than a list.
#
#   * Expo runs from apps/mobile — apps/mobile/scripts/export-web.js sets
#     `cwd: __dirname + '/..'` — so Metro loads apps/mobile/.env.local and never
#     looks at the repository root.
#   * That same wrapper falls back to a hardcoded PRODUCTION Supabase URL and
#     anon key when the variables are absent. So a value put here is not merely
#     ignored: the build succeeds and quietly targets Production.
#
# Copy the mobile template into place instead, exactly as apps/mobile/README.md
# already says:
#
#     cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env.local
#
# apps/mobile/.env.example is the authority for the Expo half and is deliberately
# NOT duplicated here. It carries context this file has no business restating —
# why EXPO_PUBLIC_MAP_WEBVIEW_BASE_URL is mandatory for a referrer-restricted
# Google key, and which existing key to reuse rather than mint a second one. A
# second copy would drift from it, and two drifting root templates are exactly
# what this file replaced.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time and tooling — set by CI, Vercel or a script, not in .env.local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA   Vercel system values; vite.config.ts and
#                                     apps/mobile/scripts/export-web.js alias
#                                     them into public build metadata
#                                     (VITE_VERCEL_ENV, VITE_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA
#                                     and their EXPO_PUBLIC_ counterparts).
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN                   OPT-IN source-map upload for the console.
#                                     When present the build emits hidden maps,
#                                     uploads them, then deletes them. SECRET —
#                                     never commit it, never prefix it VITE_.
# DOCS_BASE_REF, FORMAT_BASE_REF      Base ref for scripts/docs-check-ownership.mjs
#                                     and scripts/format-check.mjs.
# DISABLE_HMR                         Set to "true" to stop Vite watching files.
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM                 Chromium path for
#                                     scripts/build-play-screenshots.mjs.
